					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-892114#post-2066480</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-892114/fifthist-hub#post-2066480</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 09 Jul 2014 21:53:48 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>EFS19 - MC_Kejml</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1381522</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Let's see here:</p> <p>I really appreciated the spaces in the writing. Made the stuff better to read.</p> <p>The story was readable, with no major hurdles or me needing to go back and reread. Maybe the exposition was sometimes a bit forced, or overexplained. Probably that one point with MCD, UIU and COTBG being all mentioned in a short passage. It was like &quot;Hey, this is about GOIs!&quot;<br /> What I found weird how would a band like CS get to a MCD banquet.</p> <p>I liked the logo a lot, too. Makes the GoI easier to grasp, when one can imagine something connected to it.</p> <p>The Book of Dave, Uhh song and the last song were well made with flavor in mind.</p> <p>Some grammatical errors here and there; this would definitely benefit from a few rereads. Like:</p> <p>gasping, &quot;Calm (&#8230;) (should be gasping, &quot;calm (&#8230;) )</p> <p>“I’m here.” He shouted, -&gt; here,&quot; he shouted</p> <p>he following analog transmission was broadcast -&gt; was broadcasted</p> <p>And a few others.</p> <p>I have enjoyed your take on the GoI. :)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-892114#post-2060911</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-892114/fifthist-hub#post-2060911</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 30 Jun 2014 11:28:11 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1359534</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>The one thing I'm questioning is if this all really develops the GoI as much as it takes us even further away from understanding the core essence of the Fifthist Church by introducing another take on it. Does that make sense?</p> </blockquote> <p>Constellation Starfish operates in the same ways Star Signals or First Southern Fifthist does. It's a very gradual change, and their concepts evolved from something else. First Southern Fifthist, for example, were a plain old Baptist church. Constellation Starfish is a band, but they have a &quot;congregation&quot;, and the Fifthist entity speaks through them, whether they know it or not.</p> <p>The series will explain everything else, I hope. We're trying to make it less vague&#8230;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-892114#post-2060816</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-892114/fifthist-hub#post-2060816</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 30 Jun 2014 07:43:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Crayne</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1346995</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>First things first, I love every last bit of this. I love the hub, I love the entries, I love the story behind it all.</p> <p>The one thing I'm questioning is if this all really develops the GoI as much as it takes us even further away from understanding the core essence of the Fifthist Church by introducing another take on it. Does that make sense?</p> <p>I mean, I seriously love the take itself, but I can't say it's made it any clearer to me what Fifthism is actually about. :P</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
